{0 kilim}

kilim is a browser application library for OCaml. An app is a model, an
[update] function and a [view] function. The runtime writes the changes of the
view to the DOM.

{1 The libraries}

Each library has a pure part and a browser part. Use the pure part for the
modules of the app and for the tests. Use the browser part only in [main.ml].
Then kilim.testing can test the app as native code.

+ kilim: the app, the view, the tasks, the subscriptions and the components.
  See {!Kilim}.
+ kilim.browser: {!Kilim_browser.run} starts an app in a page. See
  {!Kilim_browser}.
+ kilim.testing: a fake DOM, a host with a virtual clock, pages with simulated
  events and the mocks of the libraries. See {!Kilim_testing}.
+ kilim.http and kilim.http.browser: HTTP requests as tasks, JSON and
  decoders. See {!Kilim_http} and {!Kilim_http_browser}.
+ kilim.router and kilim.router.browser: the routes of an app in the path of
  the URL. See {!Kilim_router} and {!Kilim_router_browser}.
+ kilim.websocket and kilim.websocket.browser: a WebSocket as a subscription.
  See {!Kilim_websocket} and {!Kilim_websocket_browser}.
+ kilim.storage and kilim.storage.browser: localStorage and sessionStorage as
  tasks. See {!Kilim_storage} and {!Kilim_storage_browser}.
+ kilim.web: the bindings for the Web APIs that Brr does not have. The library
  has no main module. Its units are {!Kilim_web.Es_module},
  {!Kilim_web.Js_object}, {!Kilim_web.Microtask}, {!Kilim_web.Scroll} and
  {!Kilim_web.Trusted_types}.
+ The executable [kilim] makes the page and the loader of an app, and the
  release files with content names. See
  {{:https://github.com/ocaml-caravanserai/kilim/blob/main/docs/loader.md}
  docs/loader.md}.

{1 First app}

This is [examples/counter/counter.ml]:

{@ocaml file=examples/counter/counter.ml[
(* The counter example: the model is an int. The messages change it, and the
   view shows it between two buttons. *)

open Kilim

type msg = Inc | Dec | Reset

let update n = function
  | Inc ->
      (n + 1, Cmd.none)
  | Dec ->
      (n - 1, Cmd.none)
  | Reset ->
      (0, Cmd.none)

let view n =
  El.div
    [ El.button ~at:[At.aria_label "Decrement"] ~ev:[Ev.click Dec] [txt "-"]
    ; El.output ~at:[At.data "testid" "count"] [txt (string_of_int n)]
    ; El.button ~at:[At.aria_label "Increment"] ~ev:[Ev.click Inc] [txt "+"]
    ; El.button ~ev:[Ev.click Reset] [txt "Reset"] ]

let app = App.make ~init:(fun () -> (0, Cmd.none)) ~update ~view ()
]}

[main.ml] starts the app in the element with the id [app]:

{@ocaml file=examples/counter/main.ml[
let () = Kilim_browser.run ~mount:"app" Counter.app
]}

The README of the repository tells how to build and serve the app, and how to
test it with kilim.testing.
